.TH CLI-RADIO 1 "October 2026" "cli-radio 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cli-radio \- terminal internet radio player powered by mpv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cli-radio
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
cli-radio manages personal internet radio stations in a terminal interface.
It uses mpv as its playback backend. The first normal start has an empty
station list; add stations interactively or edit the station file while
cli-radio is closed. Each station needs a unique UUID.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help and exit without starting playback or the terminal interface.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
.TP
.B Up/Down, j/k
Select a station.
.TP
.B Enter
Play or change station.
.TP
.B Space
Stop or play the selected station.
.TP
.B +, = / \-
Increase or decrease volume.
.TP
.B f
Toggle favorite.
.TP
.B /
Search station names. Enter or Esc leaves search; Esc in the main view clears
the filter.
.TP
.B a / e / d
Add, edit or delete a station. In forms, Tab and Shift+Tab change fields,
Enter saves and Esc cancels. For deletion, y confirms and n or Esc cancels
in either language.
.TP
.B r
Toggle Random mode.
.TP
.B l
Switch between German and English.
.TP
.B i
Open Info/Diagnostics without affecting playback. Press i or Esc to return.
The screen shows runtime and live buffer state, mpv version when available,
reconnect information, resolved XDG paths and useful troubleshooting commands.
Proxy credentials are never displayed. Small terminals show a runtime summary.
.TP
.B q, Ctrl+C
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cli-radio/config.toml
Settings; defaults to ~/.config/cli-radio/config.toml.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cli-radio/stations.toml
Personal stations; defaults to ~/.local/share/cli-radio/stations.toml.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cli-radio/cli-radio.log
Log; defaults to ~/.local/state/cli-radio/cli-radio.log.
.PP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME and XDG_STATE_HOME must be absolute paths.
Close cli-radio before manually editing configuration or stations.
.SH LANGUAGE
The default interface language is German. Press l to switch to English and
back. The choice is saved in config.toml.
.SH RANDOM MODE
Random mode is off by default. The r key toggles it without changing its
interval. Configure positive whole hours in config.toml:
.PP
.nf
random_mode = true
random_interval_hours = 12
.fi
.PP
Missing or invalid intervals use 12 hours. After the configured interval,
Random selects a different personal station. One station cannot switch
automatically. Reconnecting the same stream preserves the countdown.
Stop cancels it. Deliberate play, station changes, Random switches and enabling
Random during playback start a fresh interval. The mode and interval are saved;
the countdown is not persisted.
.SH PROXY ENVIRONMENT
HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY and their lowercase variants http_proxy,
https_proxy and no_proxy are supported. Lowercase values take precedence.
An explicit network.proxy setting overrides proxy environment variables.
HTTP proxies carry HTTPS streams through CONNECT. SOCKS, NTLM and Kerberos
are not supported.
.SH BUFFERING AND RELIABILITY
mpv uses approximately 10 seconds of readahead to absorb short network
interruptions. Buffering is in memory, not on disk. This is target buffering;
actual behavior depends on stream, server and network conditions, so an
interruption of exactly 10 seconds is not guaranteed to be inaudible.
Buffering is an application default and is not configurable in 0.1.1.
The Now Playing panel shows live mpv buffer duration and forward-buffered
bytes when available, and marks active buffering. Missing information is
shown as an em dash; reported values are estimates.
.PP
Playback uses --no-config, making it independent of the user's mpv.conf.
The cache settings are --cache=yes, --cache-on-disk=no, --cache-pause=yes,
--cache-pause-wait=2 and --demuxer-readahead-secs=10.
The network timeout remains 15 seconds.
.PP
A cache pause longer than 30 seconds or no playback-position progress for
60 seconds triggers the existing stalled-stream watchdog. Unexpected failures
retry without a limit, with backoff delays of 0, 1, 2, 5, 10 and then at most
30 seconds. After 60 seconds of successful playback, a later failure resets
the backoff. Intentional Stop, station or Random changes and application
shutdown do not count as disconnects or cause stale reconnects.
.SH AUTHOR
Markus Schneider.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1)
